      "content": "    327:      * Constructs a new <code>String</code> by decoding the specified array of bytes using the ISO-8859-1 charset.\n    328:      *\n    329:      * @param bytes\n    330:      *            The bytes to be decoded into characters, may be <code>null</code>\n    331:      * @return A new <code>String</code> decoded from the specified array of bytes using the ISO-8859-1 charset, or\n    332:      *         <code>null</code> if the input byte array was <code>null</code>.\n    333:      * @throws NullPointerException\n    334:      *             Thrown if {@link Charsets#ISO_8859_1} is not initialized, which should never happen since it is\n    335:      *             required by the Java platform specification.\n    336:      * @since As of 1.7, throws {@link NullPointerException} instead of UnsupportedEncodingException\n    337:      */\n    338:     public static String newStringIso8859_1(final byte[] bytes) {\n>>  339:         return new String(bytes, Charsets.ISO_8859_1);\n    340:     }\n    341: \n    342:     /**\n    343:      * Constructs a new <code>String</code> by decoding the specified array of bytes using the US-ASCII charset.\n    344:      *\n    345:      * @param bytes\n    346:      *            The bytes to be decoded into characters\n    347:      * @return A new <code>String</code> decoded from the specified array of bytes using the US-ASCII charset,\n    348:      *         or <code>null</code> if the input byte array was <code>null</code>.\n    349:      * @throws NullPointerException\n    350:      *             Thrown if {@link Charsets#US_ASCII} is not initialized, which should never happen since it is\n    351:      *             required by the Java platform specification."
